The Apache 2.0 licence at the repository root does not apply here. The root
NOTICE explains which packages are open; this file is the per-directory
boundary that licence line refers to, and it exists because a single root
licence cannot describe a repository that deliberately contains both.

What is open and what is not, and the hard rule that a feature never moves from
open to paid, are in docs/DECISIONS.md section 5.

This directory holds the channel implementations that section 5 names on the
paid side. `channels/slack.ts` is the Slack approval channel: a webhook client
that posts a held call to an operator's incoming webhook with approve and deny
buttons. It moved here from `packages/policy/src/channels/slack.ts`, which is
Apache 2.0, on 2026-10-03.

Why the implementation and not the interface. The channel interface and the
CLI channel stay open, in `packages/policy/src/channels/hold.ts` and
`channels/cli.ts`, because an open policy package that cannot notify anyone is
not complete for its purpose and would break the rule in its first week. A
paid implementation that implements an open interface is what the decision log
means by the split: the reader can see every part of the system that decides
whether an agent's write is allowed, and the vendor-specific announcement
channel is the part they pay for.

The dependency direction is one-way and a gate asserts it. This directory may
import the open core, and no open package may import this one; the test that
says so is `scripts/src/licence-line.test.mjs`, and it fails if the Slack
implementation is put back under `packages/policy`.